(room *)
(name *)	Dead end
(inherently dark *)
(look *)
	Dead end
(from * go #southwest to #ancient-chasm)

%% DEAD6
#dead-end7
(room *)
(name *)	Dead end
(inherently dark *)
(look *)
	Dead end
(from * go #east to #ancient-chasm)

%% CAVE4
#engravings-cave
(room *)
(name *)	Engravings Cave
(inherently dark *)
(look *)
	You have entered a cave with passages leading north and southeast.
(from * go #north to #round-room)
(from * go #southeast to #riddle-room)

%% RIDDL
#riddle-room
(room *)
(name *)	Riddle Room
(inherently dark *)
(look *)
	This is a room which is bare on all sides. There is an exit down. To the
	east is a great door made of stone. Above the stone, the following words
	are written:
	(par)
	'No man shall enter this room without solving this riddle:(line)
	What is tall as a house,(line)
	round as a cup,(line)
	and all the king's horses can't draw it up?'
(from * go #down to #engravings-cave)
(from * go #east to #pearl-room)
%% TODO: conditional on flag RIDDLE-FLAG
(prevent [leave * #east])
	~(riddle-flag)
		Your way is blocked by an invisible force.
(notice #door5)

(topic keyword @well)
(instead of [talk to #player about @well])
	There is a clap of thunder and the east door opens.
	(now)(riddle-flag)

%% MPEAR
#pearl-room
(room *)
(name *)	Pearl Room
(inherently dark *)
(look *)
	This is a former broom closet. The exits are to the east and west.
(from * go #east to #circular-room)
(from * go #west to #riddle-room)

%% STUDI
#studio
(room *)
(name *)	Studio
(inherently dark *)
(look *)
	You are in what appears to have been an artist's studio. The walls and
	floors are splattered with paints of 69 different colors. Strangely
	enough, nothing of value is hanging here. At the north and northwest of
	the room are open doors \(also covered with paint\). An extremely dark
	and narrow chimney leads up from a fireplace; although you might be able
	to get up it, it seems unlikely you could get back down.
(from * go #north to #north-south-crawlway)
(from * go #northwest to #gallery)
(from * go #up to #kitchen)
(prevent [leave * #up])
	~(light-load)
		The chimney is too narrow for you and all of your baggage.

%% GALLE
#gallery
(room *)
(name *)	Gallery
(look *)
	You are in an art gallery. Most of the paintings which were here have
	been stolen by vandals with exceptional taste. The vandals left through
	either the north or south exits.
(from * go #north to #west-of-chasm)
(from * go #south to #studio)

%% CAGED
#cage
(room *)
(name *)	Cage
(inherently dark *)
(look *)
	You are trapped inside an iron cage.
%% TODO: room action routine CAGED-ROOM
(narrate failing to leave * #north)
(notice #mangled-cage)

